---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Consulting"
	description="Gavin Keulks — external program review and assessment for honors programs and English departments."
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<header class="page-head">
			<h1>Consulting</h1>
			<p class="page-intro">For external program review, assessment, and curricular reform.</p>
		</header>

		<section class="lede">
			<p>
				Assessment and program review have become a more frequent part of my
				workload in post-pandemic years. I welcome such invitations and created
				the sections below to spotlight key qualifications and experiences for
				interested parties. Site visits are preferred, although I have worked
				equally effectively in virtual arrangements.
			</p>
			<p>
				I completed formal training as a program reviewer through the National
				Collegiate Honors Council&rsquo;s &ldquo;Institute for Strategic Planning,
				Assessment, and Program Review Knowledge&rdquo; (iSPARK) in 2023.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="area">
			<h2>Program Review, Assessment, and Reform</h2>
			<p>
				I have been employed as an external reviewer for honors programs in
				West&nbsp;Virginia, Montana, and Colorado &mdash; most recently the John
				F.&nbsp;Reed Honors Program at Fort&nbsp;Lewis&nbsp;College in
				spring&nbsp;2026.
			</p>
			<p>
				I have also been contracted as an English department external reviewer, most
				recently for the undergraduate and graduate programs at
				East&nbsp;Texas&nbsp;A&amp;M University &mdash; then
				Texas&nbsp;A&amp;M University&ndash;Commerce &mdash; in spring&nbsp;2024.
			</p>
			<p>
				More locally, I authored the Western Oregon University English
				department&rsquo;s self-study in autumn&nbsp;2025, co-authored the Honors
				Program&rsquo;s self-study in 2024, and co-authored the English
				department&rsquo;s earlier self-study in 2017.
			</p>
			<p>
				On two occasions, I spearheaded efforts to overhaul the WOU honors program
				curriculum, working with the honors committee and divisions across campus.
				I also led the latest revision of the English department&rsquo;s
				curriculum, working with my colleagues to consolidate three distinct majors
				into a single unified track. This represented a significant curricular
				pivot, modernizing a legacy curriculum that had existed for decades.
			</p>
			<p>
				Closely related to curriculum revision is the need to create accurate
				rearticulation strategies. Doing so prevents students from getting caught
				in-between curricula, delaying graduation (and increasing
				dissatisfaction). I have successfully managed rearticulation pathways for
				every curricular revision I have overseen.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="area">
			<h2>Statewide Service</h2>
			<ul class="record-list">
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2023&ndash;2024</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						Major Transfer Map Committee
						<span class="record-note">
							Higher Education Coordinating Commission, Oregon
						</span>
					</span>
				</li>
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2022&ndash;2023</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						Common Course Numbering Committee, literature
						<span class="record-note">
							Higher Education Coordinating Commission, Oregon
						</span>
					</span>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="area">
			<h2>Academic and Honors Advising</h2>
			<ul class="record-list papers">
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2026</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						<span class="cite-title">&ldquo;Meet Me at the Carousel: Harnessing City as Text to Build Lasting Community.&rdquo;</span>{' '}
						(With Steve Garrison and Amanda&nbsp;Threlkeld)
						<span class="record-note">
							<em>
								(Re)Reading the World: A Festschrift Celebrating 50&nbsp;Years of Place
								as Text and the Legacy of Bernice&nbsp;Braid
							</em>{' '}
							&middot; NCHC Publishing
						</span>
					</span>
				</li>
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2022</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						<span class="cite-title">Developing in Honors, opening session.</span>
						<span class="record-note">
							National Collegiate Honors Council &middot; Dallas,&nbsp;TX &middot; Panel
						</span>
					</span>
				</li>
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2022</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						<span class="cite-title">&ldquo;Honors Programs and the Humanities: the Last, Best Stand?&rdquo;</span>
						<span class="record-note">
							Scholarship of Teaching and Learning &middot; Savannah,&nbsp;GA
						</span>
					</span>
				</li>
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2021</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						<span class="cite-title">&ldquo;Working Together: Who Are Faculty Advisors and How Do They Connect with Students?&rdquo;</span>
						<span class="record-note">
							NACADA national conference &middot; Cincinnati,&nbsp;OH &middot; Panel
						</span>
					</span>
				</li>
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2018</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						<span class="cite-title">&ldquo;Advising in Honors: High Achievement, High Need, High Reward.&rdquo;</span>
